# pyenv
#   For a library or package, you might want to ignore these files since the code is
#   intended to run in multiple environments; otherwise, check them in:
# .python-version

# pipenv
#   According to pypa/pipenv#598, it is recommended to check Pipfile.lock into source control.
#   However, in case of collaboration, if having platform-specific dependencies or dependencies
#   having no cross-platform support, pipenv may install dependencies that don't work, or even
#   fail to install them on other platforms.
#Pipfile.lock

# poetry
#   Similar to Pipfile.lock, it is generally recommended to check poetry.lock in for applications.
#   But for libraries/packages, it is usually ignored.
#poetry.lock

# pdm
#   Similar to Pipfile.lock, it is generally recommended to check pdm.lock in for applications.
#.pdm-python
#pdm.lock
#pdm.toml

# PEP 582; used by e.g. github.com/pdm-project/pdm
__pypackages__/

